D11. This is my story and I'll stick to it (plur.). ~ ALIBIS
D12. Coterie. (Please note that this does not include the pantry and the vestry.) ~ SET
D17. The fellow who puts sour drops on the market. ~ BEAR
D20. A ghostly thing to do. ~ HAUNT
D22. This rules the younger generation with an iron hand. ~ SPINACH
D23. Hello, Everybody! This is one of the Smith family and she never did get that moon over the mountain. ~ KATE
D24. This kind of thing is usually a flop. ~ INERT
D27. For this it is better to use half of the recipe. ~ REC
D29. Can you remember how hot the last days of this were. ~ FOMPEII
D32. Here is where one good turn deserves another. ~ CRANK
